 <!-- /automd -->
 
+### Rotating the session password
+
+`password` accepts a list. The first entry seals every new or resealed session. The other entries are only used to open sessions sealed before the rotation. Put the new password first and keep the old one after it: swapping the order seals new sessions with the old password, with no error. Each entry must be at least 32 characters.
+
+The old password can be removed once no session sealed with it can still be valid:
+
+- With `maxAge`, after `maxAge` has passed.
+- With only `idleTimeout`, after `idleTimeout` without requests. An active session is resealed with the new password when its window slides.
+- With neither option, sessions never expire, so removing the old password signs out anyone who still has an old cookie.
+
+Sessions read from the session header are never resealed. They keep the old password until `maxAge`, or `idleTimeout` counted from the original seal.
+
 ## Fingerprint
 
