+## Rotate the Password
+
+`password` also accepts a list. The first entry seals every session, and the other entries are only tried when opening a session. To rotate the password without signing everyone out, add the new one first and keep the old one after it:
+
+```js
+import { useSession } from "h3";
+
+app.use(async (event) => {
+  const session = await useSession(event, {
+    password: [process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_NEW, process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_OLD],
+  });
+
+  // do something...
+});
+```
+
+Sessions sealed with the old password keep working and are resealed with the new one when they are next written. Remove the old password once its sessions have expired (see `maxAge` and `idleTimeout`, and the "Rotating the session password" section of the security docs). If the order is swapped, new sessions are sealed with the old password and no error is raised.
+
 ## Get Data from a Session
 
 To get data from a session, we will still use `useSession`. Under the hood, it will use `getSession` to get the session.
